      "verificationMethod": "direct-http",
      "excerpt": "January 1, 1919 - January 27, 2010. On Jan. 27, 2010, celebrated author and former Army counterintelligence agent Jerome \"J.D.\" Salinger passed away at his home in New Hampshire. Born in Manhattan on Jan. 1, 1919, Jerome David Salinger grew up in an upper-middle-class Jewish family. Salinger was assigned to the 4th CIC Detachment attached to the 4th Infantry Division. He served as an interrogator throughout the war. In his most famous work, \"The Catcher in the Rye,\" Salinger explored themes of angst, trauma, and loss of innocence.",
