      "publisher": "Penguin Random House",
      "publisherHost": "www.penguinrandomhouse.com",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "bytesRead": 168699,
      "sha256": "915fe88b18ef29066f62df01f902d9ae2e8827155bdba731f7b7ac54cbb866dd",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http",
      "excerpt": "Edward Morgan Forster was born on January 1, 1879, in London. It was not until the publication of Howards End, in 1910, that Forster achieved his first major success as a novelist. Forster first visited India during 1912 and 1913, and after a return visit in 1921, from those experiences came his most celebrated novel, A Passage to India. He died in Coventry, England, on June 7, 1970.",
      "excerptSha256": "75e36e4696ff5daac52145f185c266b32fc1dd7d5a371dfdd25491052d8495d3"
    },
